Finding: the figure leg never ran on the set. Every run's application log has 30 x "Skipping figure search: reason=noFigureTerms" and 0 x "Figure search completed":
the 30 questions carry years only ("fiscal 2026"), which figureTerms treats as no figure. So rrf-figure-weight cannot move any set metric (48 = 49 = 50, 51 = 53);
the keyword weight and k are the levers the set sees. The figure leg is judged on the NVDA figure query (below).

Rule (plan, Milestone 2; supersedes the RAG-2 ticker-only flip rule): highest hit@5 such that against BOTH 35 and 34: no ticker's hit@5 lower; no FIGURE question
that was in the top 5 under either (aapl-01, aapl-02, aapl-06, aapl-07, msft-02, msft-04, msft-10, nvda-08) leaves the top 5; hit@5 >= 0.633333. Ties: MRR, then smaller change.
  48 out: msft-04 rank 8 (rank 1 under 35).     49 out: same.     50 out: same.
  51 qualifies: tickers 0.9/0.7/0.3 >= both; the eight FIGURE questions at 1, 3, 4, 1, 2, 4, 1, 5; hit@5 0.633333.
  52 out: msft-04 rank 7.
  53 qualifies; same ranking as 51; loses the tie-break (figure weight 2.0 is the larger change from the current 0.0).
  54 out: hit@5 0.600000 < 0.633333; MSFT 0.6 < 0.7 (vs 34); msft-04 rank 7.
  => Winner id 51: rrf-k 60, rrf-vector-weight 1.0, rrf-keyword-weight 0.5, rrf-figure-weight 1.0.
  Full table with the per-question ranks of 35, 34, and 48 to 54 side by side: rule-table.txt (python over the snapshot JSONs).

Winner 51 against 35: msft-03 3->2, msft-04 1->4 (467->466), msft-05 6->3, msft-06 2->1, msft-07 miss->7, msft-10 2->1, nvda-05 miss->10; 23 unchanged.
Winner 51 against 34: aapl-06 3->4, aapl-09 10->8, msft-01 10->6, msft-02 3->2, msft-04 8->4, msft-05 2->3, msft-07 4->7, msft-10 5->1, nvda-05 miss->10, nvda-09 8->miss; 20 unchanged.
nvda-01 is a miss under 35, 34, and 51 (its question text has no figure; chunk 805 with the same totals is rank 3 under 51).

Defaults changed: application.yaml rrf-keyword-weight 0.5, rrf-figure-weight 1.0; FilingRetrievalProperties the same; FilingRetrievalServiceTests pins 1.0 / 1.0 / 0.0
in setUp for the equal-leg arithmetic tests and asserts the measured defaults in measuredDefaultsHalveTheKeywordLegAndRunTheFigureLegForNumericQueries;
RetrievalEvaluationServiceTests expects the new property values in the snapshot properties.
Floor: 0.633333 - 0.1 = 0.533333, rounded down to a multiple of 0.05 = 0.50, not higher than the current 0.50 => rag.evaluation.min-hit-at-5 stays 0.50 (comment unchanged).

